\section{What this does automatically}{

\itemize{
\item Applies the \code{\link[=ro_gg_theme]{ro_gg_theme()}} cosmetic theme.
\item Removes legend titles (RO style never shows one), for \code{fill}, \code{colour}/\code{color}, \code{shape},
\code{linetype}, \code{alpha}, and \code{size}.
\item For bar/column charts (any layer using \code{geom_col()}/\code{geom_bar()}), sets the group width to
80\% of each category slot, removes any padding between bars within the same group (switching
\code{position_dodge2()} to \code{position_dodge()} if needed), and removes bar outlines. Tick marks are
then moved from under each category to the boundary between groups via \code{\link[=ro_gg_group_ticks]{ro_gg_group_ticks()}}.
Works for both the default and flipped (\code{flip = TRUE}) orientation.
\item For bar/column and line charts (any layer using \code{geom_col()}/\code{geom_bar()}/\code{geom_line()}),
and only if the user has not already added a scale for the continuous axis, applies
\code{\link[=ro_gg_remove_axis_gap]{ro_gg_remove_axis_gap()}} expansion, \code{\link[=ro_gg_axis]{ro_gg_axis()}} as the axis limits (so the continuous axis
starts at 0), and a thousands separator on the labels. Other chart types (e.g. scatter
plots) only get the thousands separator.
\item Relocates the y-axis title to the RO position via \code{\link[=ro_gg_y_title]{ro_gg_y_title()}}, when a y-axis
title is present. Works for both the default and flipped (\code{flip = TRUE}) orientation.
